From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KintTany port maintainer <patches@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:49:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: advertise Dagor's mandatory shader draw parameters

Blades of Time's Dagor engine enumerates the host's fake Nintendo/Tegra
Vulkan device and rejects it BEFORE vkCreateDevice. The game needs both
VK_KHR_maintenance1 (already exposed) and VK_KHR_shader_draw_parameters
(not advertised) for the Vulkan vertex-ID and base-vertex semantics.

Confirmed against symbols in the actual v262144 AArch64 game main:
  drv3d_vulkan::has_all_required_extension
  drv3d_vulkan::device_has_all_required_extensions
and corresponding open-source DagorEngine/vulkan_device.cpp
(MiscRequiredExtensions<ShaderDrawParametersKHR>).

The shader draw parameters extension is promoted to Vulkan 1.1 and
declares NO extension-specific API entrypoints. The host already exposes
Vulkan 1.1, but Vulkan 1.0 applications still require the extension
name for their own device suitability checks. No shaders or features
are fabricated and no Vulkan error codes are suppressed.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Dagor BladesTime rejects physical device with unsupported required VK_KHR_shader_draw_parameters extension (Actions runs 44821228580 and 44822975454)
Issue: joao9vegeto-stack/KintTany BladesTime
---
 dm/gfx/vk/hle_vk.m | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/gfx/vk/hle_vk.m b/dm/gfx/vk/hle_vk.m
--- a/dm/gfx/vk/hle_vk.m
+++ b/dm/gfx/vk/hle_vk.m
@@ -373,6 +373,6 @@
     *count = k; return k < n ? VK_INCOMPLETE : VK_SUCCESS;
 }
 static const char *const g_inst_ext[] = {"VK_KHR_surface", "VK_NN_vi_surface", "VK_KHR_get_physical_device_properties2", "VK_KHR_get_surface_capabilities2"};
 static const char *const g_dev_ext[] = {"VK_KHR_swapchain", "VK_KHR_descriptor_update_template", "VK_KHR_maintenance1", "VK_KHR_get_memory_requirements2",
-                                        "VK_KHR_dedicated_allocation", "VK_KHR_bind_memory2"};
+                                        "VK_KHR_dedicated_allocation", "VK_KHR_bind_memory2", "VK_KHR_shader_draw_parameters"};
 static void join_names(char *out, size_t n, const char *const *names, uint32_t count) {

